---
source: src/app/space_weather_warning.rs
expression: "listed.join(\"\\n\\n\")"
---
Aircraft interference: 2 % or more of aircraft in a crossed cell reported low navigation accuracy (gpsjam.org's own yellow level).
How does aircraft interference data relate to GNSS?

Geomagnetic activity: Kp or Hp30 at 5 or higher, NOAA's G1 storm level.
How does geomagnetic activity affect GNSS?

Solar flares: class M1 or stronger, NOAA's R1 level, while the receiver was on the sunlit side.
How do solar flares affect GNSS?

TEC does not trigger a warning: no sourced level exists for an absolute TEC value. It is shown for context when a warning is active.
How does ionospheric TEC affect GNSS?
